[
  {
    "name": "__meta__",
    "issue": 2885,
    "rules": "SEMANTIC_INVARIANT (linter engine + rules)",
    "notes": [
      "Table-driven conformance vectors for the R2 structural conditions, one positive + one negative per condition (12 conditions x 2 = 24).",
      "Every vector is run THROUGH runLinter(graph, SEMANTIC_INVARIANT_RULES) so validator-channel conditions (surfaced via #2883's validateGraphIR reuse) and named-rule conditions test uniformly; the assertion filters findings by `invariant_id`.",
      "Two conditions assert `schema`-class findings (invariant_id INV-schema-valid) rather than a named rule (S7): the illegal-resource-access ENUM-MODE facet (a `mode` not in {read,write,exclusive} is pure shape, S6a) and a residual GraphIRSchema safeParse failure.",
      "Mirrors incident-derived.vectors.json / ir.vectors.json: the __meta__ element (no `graph` key) is skipped by the test.",
      "Positive graphs are deliberately minimal so the target invariant is the primary finding; a positive assertion only requires the target invariant_id to be present (extra findings are permitted). Negatives assert the target invariant_id is ABSENT."
    ]
  },

  {
    "name": "duplicate-node-ids-positive",
    "condition": "duplicate node ids",
    "invariant_id": "INV-unique-node-ids",
    "expect_flagged": true,
    "description": "Two nodes share id 'a' -> validateGraphIR duplicate_id.",
    "graph": {
      "id": "dup-pos",
      "version": "0.1",
      "nodes": [
        { "id": "a", "kind": "sequence", "terminal": true },
        { "id": "a", "kind": "sequence" }
      ],
      "edges": []
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "duplicate-node-ids-negative",
    "condition": "duplicate node ids",
    "invariant_id": "INV-unique-node-ids",
